{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/Appearance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The table follows the system look by default: system fonts and colors,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alternating row backgrounds, a rounded selection like the Finder sidebar,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overlay scrollers, light and dark mode, the user’s accent color, and a Liquid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Glass summary bar on macOS 26 (a header material on earlier systems). Rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scroll underneath the summary bar.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Sizes","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Sizes"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Property"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Default"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"24"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rows’ height, unless the delegate gives rows their own ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableViewRowHeights"},{"type":"text","text":") or a column wraps text (then the height of a row of one line)."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/headerRowHeight"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"28"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The column titles."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/groupHeaderHeight"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"24"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The group band, only shown when there are groups."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryRowHeight"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"30"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The summary row."}]}]]]},{"text":"Fonts, colors and density","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Fonts-colors-and-density"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The table uses the system fonts and colors, following light and dark mode,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accent color and contrast settings. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/tableStyle","isActive":true},{"text":" changes them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where an app needs its own look; anything left ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays the system’s:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["table.tableStyle = GHTableStyle(","    fontSize: 15,                      \/\/ cells and the summary row","    headerFontSize: 12,                \/\/ column titles","    textColor: .labelColor,","    backgroundColor: NSColor(named: \"TableBackground\"),","    stripeColors: [.clear, NSColor(named: \"Stripe\")!],","    groupRowColor: NSColor(named: \"GroupRow\"))","table.density = .compact               \/\/ or .regular (24 points), .spacious"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/density","isActive":true},{"text":" sets ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight","isActive":true},{"text":" for the style’s font,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a little, some or more room around the text, like Finder’s list sizes;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it follows a later font size change. Give the style the same color objects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each time (the renderer resolves each color once per appearance).","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Rows and selection","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Rows-and-selection"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/usesAlternatingRowBackgroundColors"},{"type":"text","text":" stripes the rows with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s alternating content colors."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/showsVerticalGridLines"},{"type":"text","text":" draws thin lines between columns."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/selectionHighlightStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":".rounded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (inset, rounded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corners, like macOS lists; the table then keeps a small margin at its edges)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"code":".fullWidth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (a plain band across the whole row, like classic tables)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The selection is shown in the accent color while the table is focused and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in gray otherwise."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Highlighting rows by their data","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Highlighting-rows-by-their-data"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The delegate can tint a row’s background and put a colored marker at its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leading edge, for example green for profitable campaigns and red for losing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ones:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Created once: the table asks for every visible row while scrolling.","static let profitTint = NSColor.systemGreen.withAlphaComponent(0.10)","static let lossTint = NSColor.systemRed.withAlphaComponent(0.10)","","func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, backgroundColorForRow row: Int) -> NSColor? {","    let roi = data.campaigns[row].roi","    return roi > 0 ? Self.profitTint : roi < 0 ? Self.lossTint : nil","}","","func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, markerColorForRow row: Int) -> NSColor? {","    data.campaigns[row].isOverBudget ? .systemOrange : nil","}"]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use light, translucent tints so text stays readable, and return the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"color objects every time (static constants): the table compares them to skip"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unchanged rows."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tints replace the alternating stripes of their rows. Selected rows show the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection instead of the tint, and keep the marker."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"System colors like "},{"code":"systemGreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" adapt to dark mode and accent changes by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table asks when rows come into view and on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/reloadData()"},{"type":"text","text":". If the condition behind a tint changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without a data change, call "},{"code":"reloadData()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Empty state","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Empty-state"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While there are no rows, the table shows "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/emptyStateText","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your own "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/emptyStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (for example with a button to create"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the first record). The table places it; the app says what it is."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without any data (the data source has no rows), the table shows only the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty state, centered: no header, row stripes or summary row."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowFilter"},{"type":"text","text":" hides every row, the columns stay and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty state shows in the rows area. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/FilteringAndSearch"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While the data updates (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/isUpdatingData"},{"type":"text","text":"), the spinner"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes its place, and it comes back if there are still no rows. There’s no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"need to clear the text while loading."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Scrolling","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Scrolling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table scrolls by itself, like a scroll view:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"trackpads scroll with momentum and bounce at the top and bottom; turn the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bounce off with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/bouncesVertically"},{"type":"text","text":";"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"gestures lock to the axis they start on, so vertical scrolling doesn’t drift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sideways;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"overlay scrollers appear while scrolling and expand under the pointer;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with “Show scroll bars: Always” in System Settings, the table shows classic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scrollers that take up space;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"clicking the scroller track pages, and holding it keeps paging;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"scrolling on an axis the table has nothing to scroll on goes to the view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that contains it, like a nested scroll view’s: a table of a few rows in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form scrolls the form (alone in a window, its rows still bounce)."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In code, read "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and scroll with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/scroll(to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/scrollRowToVisible(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didScrollNotification","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tells every change of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" once the rows are laid out there, where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NSTableView apps watch the clip view’s bounds: for example, load the next"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"page when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rowIndexes(in: table.bounds)"},{"type":"text","text":" reaches the last rows."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/willStartLiveScrollNotification","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didLiveScrollNotification","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didEndLiveScrollNotification","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" follow the user’s scrolling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like a scroll view’s: a trackpad gesture or a drag of the overlay scroller,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ending with its momentum. Never make"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the table the document of an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSScrollView"},{"type":"text","text":" (a form around it in one is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fine)."}]},{"text":"Localization","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Localization"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table’s own texts — its menus (the summary scope, columns, grouping,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"views), the column filter and save view dialogs, Undo names and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"VoiceOver reads — are localized in English and Russian; the summary scope"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"titles can be replaced with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryScopeTitles"},{"type":"text","text":". Everything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else the user reads — column"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"titles, tool tips, menus, empty state texts, tags and mark labels — comes from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your app, localized as you like. Numbers and dates are formatted in the user’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"locale."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Right-to-left languages","anchor":"Right-to-left-languages"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a right-to-left interface (Arabic, Hebrew; the table follows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/userInterfaceLayoutDirection"},{"type":"text","text":", which AppKit sets from the app’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"language) the whole table is mirrored, like AppKit’s own controls:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first column is at the right; leading frozen columns stay at the right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge and trailing ones at the left; the vertical scroller is at the left."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each cell’s content is mirrored within it: leading text at the right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbers aligned to the trailing side (the left), tags listed from the right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data bars growing from the right, outline and group indents and their"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disclosure triangles at the right, the triangles of collapsed rows pointing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left. Text itself reads as written: every line moves whole, so Arabic,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Hebrew and mixed text keep their order.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Column titles put the filter button and the sort arrow at their left;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"columns resize from their left edge and move by dragging the other way."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Left Arrow goes to the next column and Right Arrow back (on group headers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and tree rows, Right Arrow collapses and Left Arrow expands); Tab still goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the next column. Swiping a row to the right shows its trailing actions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the left."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" still counts from the leading end: 0 shows the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first columns, at the right. Printing and PDF put the first column at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right too."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"code":"userInterfaceLayoutDirection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself to show one table mirrored or not,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whatever the app’s language."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Appearance","modules":[{"name":"Gingham"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gingham\/appearance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Adjust sizes, highlight rows by their data, and choose how selection and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scrolling look.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/KeyboardAndAccessibility","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHSelectionHighlightStyle","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableStyle","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableDensity"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Appearance-and-Behavior","title":"Appearance and Behavior"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham"]]},"references":{"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/summaryScopeTitles":{"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/summaryscopetitles","title":"summaryScopeTitles","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"summaryScopeTitles","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"GHSummaryScope","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Gingham14GHSummaryScopeO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryScopeTitles","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Titles of the summary row context menu, localized (English, Russian) by default."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/rowHeight":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rowHeight","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CGFloat","preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"rowHeight","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Height of every row, in points (at least 1), unless the delegate gives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows heights of their own ("},{"code":"GHTableViewRowHeights","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") or a column wraps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text ("},{"code":"GHTableColumn.wrappingText()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": a row of one line has it, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"line more adds the font’s line height); group header rows have it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any case."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight","url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/rowheight"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/rowFilter":{"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/rowfilter","title":"rowFilter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rowFilter","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GHRowFilter","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Gingham11GHRowFilterV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowFilter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows shown, e.g. for a search field. Row indexes in the API (selection,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delegate and data source calls) stay data source indexes; summaries,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection, copying and VoiceOver only cover the rows shown. When the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data changes, call "},{"code":"reloadData()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (it filters again), or a targeted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"update (it filters the changed rows again; the other rows keep their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match); set the filter again when only the condition behind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isIncluded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" changed. "},{"code":"isIncluded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is kept by the table: capture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" weakly in it. The first search of a large table reads its words"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the background (see "},{"code":"synchronousSearchLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/didLiveScrollNotification":{"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/didlivescrollnotification","title":"didLiveScrollNotification","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"didLiveScrollNotification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Notification","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12NotificationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Name","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12NotificationV4Namea","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didLiveScrollNotification","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Posted after each step of a live scroll (with "},{"code":"didScrollNotification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like "},{"code":"NSScrollView.didLiveScrollNotification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/didEndLiveScrollNotification":{"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/didendlivescrollnotification","title":"didEndLiveScrollNotification","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"didEndLiveScrollNotification","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Notification","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12NotificationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Name","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12NotificationV4Namea","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Posted when a live scroll ended, its momentum too, like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"NSScrollView.didEndLiveScrollNotification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": e.g. to load what came"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into view."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didEndLiveScrollNotification","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/summa